Usage: raphael list <path>... [options]
       raphael list --id <id> [options]

List children of one or more paths or ids.

Use / for the root. Mix paths and repeated --id, up to 10 distinct places. A note has no children and returns an empty page.

Direct children are listed by default. -r includes all descendants. Ordering applies before paging.

Rules:
  The default page contains at most 50 results. --limit accepts 1–500; --skip skips results. At most 10 paths or ids may be searched or listed in one request.
  --order-by accepts slug, updatedAt, id with asc or desc; for example --order-by updatedAt:desc.
  --filter accepts a JSON object with keys type, kind, tags. Allowed type values: area, project, resource. Allowed kind values: note. Each value is a scalar or {"$in":[...]}; sibling keys are ANDed. Tags match at least one supplied tag, with exact case after trimming and NFC normalization. A kind does not imply a type.

Options:
      --id <id>
      Include this id alongside positional paths. Repeatable.
      --filter <json|@file>
      JSON object. Keys: type, kind, tags. Values may use {"$in":[...]}. See help addressing.
      --skip <n>
      Number of results to skip. Default: 0.
      --limit <n>
      Page size, 1 to 500. Default: 50.
      --include-archived
      Include archived items.
  -r, --recursive
      Include all descendants.
      --order-by <field:direction>
      Repeat in priority order. Fields: slug, updatedAt, id. Directions: asc, desc. Repeatable. Default: slug:asc then id:asc.
      --json
      Print one JSON result.
  -h, --help
      Show this help.

Examples:
  raphael list /
  raphael list / -r --filter '{"type":"resource"}' --order-by updatedAt:desc --limit 4
  raphael list /work /personal --filter '{"tags":{"$in":["urgent"]}}'

Prints:
  One row per item. JSON carries `items` and `page`; paging notes go to stderr.

Next: raphael get --id 42

See also: raphael help addressing; raphael help output

---

Usage: raphael search <path>... -q <query> [options]
       raphael search --id <id> -q <query> [options]

Search all descendants by text.

Search is recursive by default; use --direct for direct children only. Search everything with raphael search / -q auth. Matching includes titles, descriptions and note text. Repeat -q to OR queries together, at most 10 queries. Each query allows at most 1000 characters and 32 words or quoted phrases. Adjacent words mean OR; uppercase AND binds more tightly than uppercase OR. Double quotes make a phrase. Operators need a word or phrase on both sides. Lowercase and and or are ordinary search words. There are no parentheses, NOT, wildcards or field prefixes. Matching ignores case and accents; there is no stemming: token does not match tokens. Punctuation separates words: auth* matches auth, not authentication.

Results are ordered by relevance; --order-by is not accepted.

Rules:
  The default page contains at most 50 results. --limit accepts 1–500; --skip skips results. At most 10 paths or ids may be searched or listed in one request.
  --filter accepts a JSON object with keys type, kind, tags. Allowed type values: area, project, resource. Allowed kind values: note. Each value is a scalar or {"$in":[...]}; sibling keys are ANDed. Tags match at least one supplied tag, with exact case after trimming and NFC normalization. A kind does not imply a type.

Options:
      --id <id>
      Include this id alongside positional paths. Repeatable.
      --filter <json|@file>
      JSON object. Keys: type, kind, tags. Values may use {"$in":[...]}. See help addressing.
      --skip <n>
      Number of results to skip. Default: 0.
      --limit <n>
      Page size, 1 to 500. Default: 50.
      --include-archived
      Include archived items.
  -q, --query <text>
      Text to search. At least one required. Repeatable.
      --direct
      Search direct children only.
      --json
      Print one JSON result.
  -h, --help
      Show this help.

Examples:
  raphael search / -q auth
  raphael search /work -q '"login flow" AND retry'
  raphael search /work /personal -q auth --limit 20
  raphael search /work --direct -q auth --filter '{"type":"resource","kind":"note"}'

Prints:
  One row per match, with closest matches first. JSON carries `items[].node` and `page`.

Next: raphael get --id 42

See also: raphael help addressing; raphael help output

